task(OMEGA-MARGIN-DIAG):
  title    = "omega.margin ≡ 0.0 in every kernel_tick — uninformative boundary signal"
  status   = deployed
                       // margin_free emitted + varies. RESIDUAL binder → task(OMEGA-MARGIN-BINDING-DIAG).
  priority = alta  // RAISED 2026-07-02: the Fierro bridge doc PROMISES omega.margin
                   // as the observable ε_frontier of Q1 — must be fixed or disclosed
                   // before the Q4 send (see fierro_q4_package.vsm pre_send_checklist)
  date     = "2026-07-02"
  owner    = "DS [S] (diagnosis guided below)"
  context:
    "Every observed kernel_tick (June AND July builds) reports omega.margin=0.0 with
     viable=true. min_distance_to_boundary(&state)==0.0 constantly means some dimension
     sits EXACTLY on an Ω boundary (e.g. a dim clamped at a box bound like 0.0) — so the
     margin carries no early-warning information and any drift detector on it is blind.
     Diagnose: extend omega_validator (or a one-off test on 108) to report WHICH
     constraint attains the minimum; if it is a structurally-pinned dim (clamped output),
     exclude it from the margin or report margin over free dims separately.
     Value: margin becomes a usable early-warning signal for CHECO-PROJ ttb estimates."
  files    = [projects/vsf-nucleus/src/omega_validator.rs, projects/vsf-nucleus/src/operational.rs]
  // ── DIAGNOSIS 2026-07-02 (Claude/Fable, live-confirmed on LXC 101) ───────────
  diagnosis:
    "ROOT CAUSE: BoxConstraint::distance_to_boundary uses NEAREST-face distance
     min(v-lo, hi-v). At the healthy operating point several dims sit exactly ON
     (or within eps of) a box face, so the global min collapses to 0.0 — an artifact
     of representation bounds, NOT dynamical proximity to danger.
     Live kernel_tick (tick 66, 2026-07-02T16:08Z, events.jsonl@101) confirms the
     pinning dims (omega.margin=0.0, viable=true):
       - governed=1.0        (dim13, categorical {0,1}) -> on hi face of [0,1]   -> dist 0.0
       - lifecycle=1.0       (dim15, production max)     -> on hi face of [0.2,1] -> dist 0.0
       - mem_pressure=0.0    (healthy = no pressure)     -> on lo face of [0,1]   -> dist 0.0
       - stasis_cos=0.999884 (healthy ~ perfect stasis)  -> eps from hi of [-1,1] -> dist 1.16e-4
     So min is structurally 0.0 whenever the system is HEALTHY. Precedent: the module
     already excludes A0/A0.1 (dims 53/54) from canonical() for this exact reason —
     'distance=0 at the good state would incorrectly dominate g' (omega_validator.rs:13-19)."
  fix_decision:  // NEEDS rmw3/S5 ratification — it defines what 'margin' means in the Fierro Q4 submission
    "RECOMMENDED: directional (danger-face) margin, not nearest-face.
      (1) Exclude categorical/validity gates (governed, lifecycle) from the margin
          entirely — they belong to is_member (validity), never to early-warning.
      (2) For continuous box dims, measure distance to the DANGER face only:
          pressures/H_t/H_rest -> hi ; budget/cgroup_headroom/trust_hist/stasis_cos -> lo.
      (3) Emit a NEW omega.margin_free alongside the existing viable+margin (keep
          margin for chain-format continuity; margin_free is the informative signal).
     ALTERNATIVE (minimal): DISCLOSE in the Fierro cover that omega.margin is currently a
     validity indicator (0.0 = on-boundary-by-design, viable=true) and the continuous
     eps_frontier is future work. Fix is tractable (~half day DS) and strictly better;
     recommend FIX over disclose."
  handoff:
    "DS [S] once ratified: add danger-face metadata to BoxConstraint + Omega::margin_free()
     + wire operational.rs:1038 to also emit omega.margin_free; build on 108, cert, deploy 101.
     GATE: rmw3 ratifies the danger-face modeling choice before impl (feeds the Q4 claim)."
  // ── DEPLOYED 2026-07-02 (Claude/Fable) ───────────────────────────────────────
  deployed:
    "rmw3/S5 ratified the fix. DangerFace{Lo,Hi,Both,Skip} + Constraint::margin_distance +
     Omega::margin_free wired; operational.rs emits omega.margin_free. Built on 108
     (bin 8f33863c, GLIBC≤2.34), 11/11 omega_validator tests green (incl. 2 new
     regressions), cutover to 101 with R4 (old pid 1030137 confirmed gone), state.db
     deploy recorded. Commits: 4288364 (src) + this. Restart created the expected chain
     seam (tick reset 162→1, prev_hash=null → one merkle_break sev10, NUCLEUS-CHAIN-RESTART-SEAM).
     LIVE-VERIFIED: margin_free now emitted and rises monotonically during warmup
     (tick1=0.0 tr=0.825 → tick4=1.29e-4 tr=0.894); categorical gates no longer pin it."
  residual:
    "margin_free settles near ~1e-4 even at trust≈0.9 — so the binder is NOT trust and NOT
     the (excluded) gates; almost certainly normalized entropy H_t/H_rest sitting near its
     Hi danger face in the chronic 'degen' phase (h_t raw≈1.9-2.0). Either an honest
     'near entropy ceiling' signal OR a relocated pin (if the entropy normalization
     saturates at ~1.0 in normal operation). Undercuts the early-warning value for OTHER
     dims (their drift is masked by the ~1e-4 entropy floor). Follow-up below."

task(ENTROPY-SATURATION-REVIEW):   // P2
  title    = "H_T saturates in degen — entropy dim reflects INTERNAL relaxation, not external danger"
  status   = open
  priority = media
  date     = "2026-07-02"
  owner    = "Claude/Fable design ([O]) → DS [S] impl + rmw3 [H] semantics call"
  context:
    "H_T = Shannon entropy of the kernel's INTERNAL 4-state Boltzmann distribution p
     (kernel_step.rs step(): p = 0.99*p + 0.01*p_eq(kt_eff)); h_max=log2(4)=2. Chronic degen
     (h_t≈1.9-2.0, normalized≈1.0) has two causes: (i) the 0.99 contraction is slow (~460 ticks
     to 99% of p_eq) and (ii) every restart resets p→[0.25;4] = uniform = MAX entropy. So H_T
     tracks the kernel's own self-organization, NOT an external viability danger."
  design:
    "(A) [S] persist p (+ h_rest EMA) across restarts — checkpoint the kernel dist to /var/lib/vsf
         and reload on boot; removes the reset-to-max-entropy transient (complements P5 seam).
     (B) [O/S] margin role: since H_T is internal-relaxation not external-danger, DROP it from the
         margin_free danger set (danger=Both or Skip) — folds into OMEGA-MARGIN-BINDING-DIAG.
     (C) [H] rmw3/S5: is a 4-symbol alphabet (h_max=2 bits) + a degen-dominant regime intended,
         or should the variety be widened / relaxation sped up? Kernel-semantics decision."
  files    = [projects/vsf-nucleus/src/kernel_step.rs, projects/vsf-nucleus/src/omega_validator.rs]
  audit_2026_08_02: "2026-08-02 debt audit: part (A) CONFIRMED done — kernel_step.rs has a
      checkpoint_path field + Checkpoint struct explicitly commented 'ENTROPY-SATURATION-REVIEW
      P2-A'. Part (B) was flagged unverified by the audit; resolved same-day by direct source
      read: omega_validator.rs:395-397 margin_free() doc comment reads verbatim 'EXCLUDES H_T
      (normalized entropy) from the min because it structurally saturates near 1.0 in chronic
      degen ... masking early-warning from all other dims' — matches this task's own design
      rationale for (B) exactly. margin_free_binding() excludes it too (line 407-408). CONFIRMED
      DONE, live in source, not just claimed in a session log. Only (C) remains: rmw3's own
      semantics call (widen the 4-symbol alphabet or accept degen-dominant as intended) — not
      DS-executable, task stays open on (C) alone."

