              entra en una zona fuera de omega'"
  context:
    "The Jun-26 8G→1G downsize silently killed Qwen because memory for the LLM is a
     static pct-set value with no viability feedback. Design: extend DS's
     s3_resource_alloc.py so that an Ω-boundary signal (e.g. S4-layer dark: canary
     integrity=failed streak, or omega.margin degradation in φ↑) triggers a memory
     grant large enough for the model (~5 GB), and reclaim only when the LLM is
     verifiably idle/unloaded — never below what the loaded model needs. Requires:
     (a) pool sizing rethink (current pool 1536 MB << one model), (b) a grant class
     with a floor tied to a service requirement, not just stress depth, (c) R10
     respected — the grant path is S3 resource bargain, no LLM in the loop.
     Spec first (experiment_spec pattern), then DS [S] implements."
  depends_on = ["s3_resource_alloc.py source sync (see A0-ALLOC-BASELINE-SYNC)"]
  audit_2026_08_02: "CONFIRMED genuinely still open (2026-08-02 debt audit): P1 (grant mechanism)
      done 2026-07-02, P2 (startup assert) + P3 (state.db-backing) explicitly named 'next' and
